<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina's Telecom Q2 net $71 mln vs $70 mln.</title>
<headline>Argentina's Telecom Q2 net $71 mln vs $70 mln.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Period to March 31.</p>
<p>Earnings per share: $0.072 vs n/a.</p>
<p>Net income:  $71 million vs $70 million</p>
<p>Revunues: $503 million vs $467 million</p>
<p>NOTE: Telecom, with about 46 percent of the domestic market, is Argentina's second-largest phone company.</p>
<p>It is controlled with a 60 percent stake by Nortel Inversora SA, formed by Italy's STET (32.5 percent), France Telecom unit France Cable et Radio (32.5 percent), Argentine conglomerate Perez Companc (25 percent) and J.P. Morgan (10 percent).</p>
<p>((-Guillermo Hskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
